# Code Review Checklist
# Applies: ALL projects (user-level)
# Purpose: Default code review checklist when user asks for review/audit

## Review Dimensions

### 1. Correctness
- [ ] Does the code do what it claims?
- [ ] Are edge cases handled?
- [ ] Are error paths tested?
- [ ] Is there correct input validation?

### 2. Security
- [ ] User input sanitized/validated?
- [ ] No SQL injection, XSS, CSRF vulnerabilities?
- [ ] Secrets not hardcoded?
- [ ] Proper authorization checks?
- [ ] Rate limiting where needed?

### 3. Performance
- [ ] N+1 query issues?
- [ ] Unnecessary memory allocations?
- [ ] Synchronous blocking in async code?
- [ ] Proper indexing on database queries?

### 4. Maintainability
- [ ] Clear, descriptive naming?
- [ ] Functions do one thing?
- [ ] No deeply nested logic?
- [ ] Constants extracted?
- [ ] Magic numbers avoided?

### 5. Testing
- [ ] Unit test coverage for new logic?
- [ ] Edge cases tested?
- [ ] Mocks/stubs used correctly?
- [ ] Tests are deterministic?

### 6. Type Safety
- [ ] No `any` types without justification?
- [ ] Proper type annotations?
- [ ] Generic types used correctly?

### 7. Error Handling
- [ ] Errors caught and handled?
- [ ] Meaningful error messages?
- [ ] Errors propagated correctly?
- [ ] No silent failures?

### 8. Federated Systems (if applicable)
- [ ] ActivityPub compatibility?
- [ ] AP actor/object format correct?
- [ ] Rate limiting on federation?
- [ ] Inbox delivery handling?

### 9. Job Queue / Async (if applicable)
- [ ] Job failures handled with retry?
- [ ] Dead letter queue configured?
- [ ] Job deduplication?
- [ ] Idempotent job handlers?
